{"id":"asp-or-adder","name":"Asp, Or Adder","aliases":["Asp"],"sources":["torrey","easton"],"topics":["torrey:asp-or-adder"],"groups":[],"definition":{"source":"easton","term":"Asp","text":"(Heb. pethen), Deut. 32:33; Job 20:14, 16; Isa. 11:8. It was probably the Egyptian cobra (Naja haje), which was very poisonous (Rom. 3:13; Gr. aspis). The Egyptians worshipped it as the uraeus, and it was found in the desert and in the fields. The peace and security of Messiah’s reign is represented by the figure of a child playing on the hole of the asp. (See ADDER.)"},"lemmas":[{"strong":"H6620","lemma":"פֶּתֶן","xlit":"pethen","gloss":"an asp","kjv":"adder","count":6,"share":0.5},{"strong":"H5175","lemma":"נָחָשׁ","xlit":"nâchâsh","gloss":"a snake","kjv":"serpent","count":4,"share":0.33},{"strong":"H6848","lemma":"צֶפַע","xlit":"tsephaʻ","gloss":"a viper","kjv":"adder, cockatrice","count":2,"share":0.17},{"strong":"H2534","lemma":"חֵמָה","xlit":"chêmâh","gloss":"heat","kjv":"anger, bottles, hot displeasure, furious","count":3,"share":0.25},{"strong":"H7219","lemma":"רֹאשׁ","xlit":"rôʼsh","gloss":"a poisonous plant, probably the poppy","kjv":"gall, hemlock, poison, venom","count":2,"share":0.17},{"strong":"H5391","lemma":"נָשַׁךְ","xlit":"nâshak","gloss":"to strike with a sting","kjv":"bite, lend upon usury","count":2,"share":0.17}],"verses":["Deut.32.33","Job.20.14","Job.20.16","Ps.58.4","Ps.91.13","Isa.11.8","Gen.49.17","Ps.58.5","Ps.140.3","Prov.23.32","Isa.11.9","Rom.3.13"],"related":[{"id":"asp","type":"cooccur","shared":8,"jaccard":0.667,"why":"8 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"adder","type":"cooccur","shared":5,"jaccard":0.417,"why":"5 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"serpent","type":"cooccur","shared":7,"jaccard":0.13,"why":"7 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"reptiles","type":"cooccur","shared":5,"jaccard":0.114,"why":"5 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"serpents","type":"cooccur","shared":4,"jaccard":0.087,"why":"4 verses are indexed under both"